regress\artifacts\lcaconfwidth\grok_witness2_20260907.txt:32:Do **not** `put d` the killing value *at the device*. `store_64bit_word` goes through `memory_rw` with `CACHE_DATA` and **no** `NO_EXCEPTIONS`, so that path *does* enter `dev_lca_ioc_access` and will `exit(1)` from the debugger. That is not a guest instruction and is not rung-3.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfwidth\grok_witness2_20260907.txt:80:**Distinguish from the other ten live `exit(1)` sites by text, never by status.** The unique pin is `unimplemented bit of IOC_CONF`. The two interrupt stubs print `lca_interrupt_assert: TODO` / `lca_interrupt_deassert: TODO`. Under `-V` they also cannot fire by delivery (`cpu_dyntrans.c` suppresses interrupts while single-stepping), and this store does not assert them synchronously. Default-arm text is `[ lca_ioc: unimplemented write to offset 0x...`. Do not grep bare `TODO` or bare `IOC_CONF`.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfwidth\grok_witness2_20260907.txt:103:This round is the specifier. It does not remove `exit(1)`, and it does not undo the store-before-guard. Those are `lcabadval`.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfwidth\grok_witness2_20260907.txt:112:4. **Store-before-guard:** after a printf-only fix the 64-bit value is still committed to `d->ioc_conf` before death. PCI decode uses only bit 0, so it is currently unused — a `lcabadval` disposition fact, not a reason to widen this round.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfwidth\grok_census_20260907.txt:174:	default:fatal("[ lca_ioc: unimplemented %s to offset 0x%x",
regress\artifacts\lcaconfwidth\grok_census_20260907.txt:340:**70 files.****VERDICT: S3’s 226 is the no-space correlate and is right for that command; S3’s 15 is a string-proximity correlate that is wrong in both directions at once. The real class is much smaller: one LIVE member (`dev_lca.c` IOC_CONF) plus about six CODE members that are latent or unattached. S4 is the right discriminator if you add a reachability tag. `dev_lca.c:313` and `dev_mvme187.c:88` are not members. This is not a prerequisite of `lcabadval`. `PRIx64` is already the house idiom in this same function.**
regress\artifacts\lcaconfwidth\grok_census_20260907.txt:444:**The obvious form is already in this file.** Five sibling value-guard `fatal()`s in `dev_lca_ioc` use:
regress\artifacts\lcaconfwidth\grok_census_20260907.txt:454:**Blast radius of fixing IOC_CONF only: none measured.** Grep of `regress/*.{py,sh,c}` and `tools/*.{py,sh,c}` finds **no** match on `IOC_CONF`, `unimplemented bit of`, `IGS_VDO flags`, `FE_BMPR16`, `STCR byte`, or `extdma magic`. No current probe, hygiene grep, or gate keys on that text. A future `lcabadval` row that matches the unique phrase `"unimplemented bit of IOC_CONF"` (not the hex) will not invert when the specifier widens. A row that matches the full string including a 32-bit-only hex would.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfwidth\grok_census_20260907.txt:460:## Q5 — ordering vs `lcabadval`
regress\artifacts\lcaconfwidth\grok_census_20260907.txt:469:- Alpha `stl` of `0x2` is a 32-bit store: high bits stay 0, print is accurate, host still dies. That is a complete IOC_CONF row for `lcabadval`’s “unimplemented bits kill” claim.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfwidth\grok_census_20260907.txt:471:`lcaconfwidth` is a **sibling** whose own witness is the `stq`/`put d` of `0x100000000` and a check that the log says `0x100000000` rather than `0x0`. That row is this defect; it is not owed before `lcabadval` can be built.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfwidth\grok_census_20260907.txt:479:1. **IOC_CONF stores before the guard** (`d->ioc_conf = idata` then `if (idata & ~1)`). A distinguishing write still kills, but the 64-bit value is already in device state. That is a `lcabadval` disposition fact (decline-that-keeps-the-store is an accept), not this row.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfwidth\CENSUS_brief.md:33:**S2 — WHY IT IS NOT COSMETIC, and this is why the row exists.** A sibling HIGH row, `lcabadval`,
