regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\SELFREVIEW_brief.md:81:**Q5. Scope.** You listed `lca_ioc`'s default arm, the two interrupt handlers and `lca_isa`'s guard
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_minimax.txt:1:**VERDICT**: **A for all six.** Premise 6 is conditionally sound — it holds IF premise 2 holds (no fourth read of the five window/TB_ENA fields). The brief treats all six as one block, but **CONF is structurally different** (it has a consumer: `bus = d->ioc_conf & 1` in `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_pci_conf)`), and the argument for the five doesn't transfer cleanly. For the five, A is right because there is no consumer to protect and A preserves register-file fidelity (write X, read X, which hardware does). For CONF, A is *even more clearly* right: the consumer uses only bit 0, so storing a rejected value leaves the consumer correct; **B can silently break the consumer** if the old `ioc_conf` had a different bit 0. B is the wrong fix everywhere. The single fact that decides the fork is premise 2 — whether any tree code reads the five fields outside their readback sites.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_kimi.txt:55:Two facts settle it, both cheap: (1) which machine file under `GXEMUL-SEC/src/` instantiates `dev_lca` and at what physical base (one grep for the init call); (2) the values of `LCA_IOC_BASE` and `LCA_IOC_W_MASK0` (the header). If both exist, a rung-3 debugger store of any value `!= 0x700000` to `machine_base + (LCA_IOC_W_MASK0 - LCA_IOC_BASE)` reaches the arm through real decode; the probe need not match any real guest's value stream, so envelope violation is free. If no machine instantiates the device, it is documented-only.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_glm.txt:6:- **P2 — stated, NOT CHECKABLE from the packet.** Only `lca_ioc` is inlined; the tree-wide counts and the `lca_pci_conf` consumer line are asserted. The `ioc_conf` count of 4 is internally coherent with the packet (2 inlined uses + declaration + 1 consumer); the fives' counts of 3 are coherent but unproven. Settling fact: a scoped search for reads of `window_base_0/1`, `window_mask_0/1`, `tlb_enable`. One caveat the panel should not skip: a bare grep for `tlb_enable` may hit other devices' fields, so "exactly 3, whole tree" is only meaningful if scoped to `struct lca_data`. Re-run with the scoping stated — this is exactly the class of count this panel ratified wrongly before.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_glm.txt:36:- **READ:** `default:` still prints and exits for reads AND writes (inlined). "Firmware can still terminate" is trivially right via any unhandled offset — `lca_ioc` itself stays lethal.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_glm.txt:38:- Within `lca_ioc` the six guards plus `default:` are all exit paths, so pass 1 does close the value guards inside this one function.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\grok.txt:29:4. **B’s readback lie is the one hardware never tells, and it fires on documented encodings.** Past the packet, `alpha_lcareg.h` defines `IOC_W_MASK_1M` as `0x0` and `IOC_W_BASE_WEN` as bit 33. The model accepts:
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\grok.txt:33:   | `W_MASK0` | `0x700000` | `IOC_W_MASK_8M` only |
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\grok.txt:34:   | `W_MASK1` | `0x3ff00000` | `IOC_W_MASK_1G` only |
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\grok.txt:82:| `default:` | **both** reads and writes, including `LCA_IOC_STAT0` / `STAT1` and every other offset in the 512 MB `lca_ioc` window |
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\grok.txt:102:Past the packet: `regress/lca_confwidth_probe.py` already issued a guest `stq`/`ldq` through that decode at CONF on unmodified `alphabook1`. The other five are other cases of the same `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc)` on the same mapping. Three probe traps that file already paid for, so a new one does not rediscover them: debugger `dump` skips `DM_DEFAULT` handlers; debugger `put d` of a killing value *is* a host kill but is not a guest instruction; HAE at window offset 0 silently succeeds, so a miss control must not use `LCA_IOC_BASE+0`.
