regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:19:**S2’s six predicates hold.** They are exactly the `if (idata` tests in `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc)`. Three accept one value (`W_MASK0` `{0x700000}`, `W_BASE1` `{0x240000000}`, `W_MASK1` `{0x3ff00000}`); three accept two (`IOC_CONF` `{0,1}`, `TB_ENA` `{0,0x80}`, `W_BASE0` `{0, 0x300800000}`).
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:25:**S4 is right about the machine, slightly overclaimed about the six arms.** `machine_alpha.c` adds `"lca"` only under `ST_ALPHABOOK1`. `lca_confwidth_probe.py` has driven a guest `stq` into `LCA_IOC_CONF` on stock `alphabook1`. That proves the **device window**. The other five labels are the same `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc)` at header offsets inside a `0x20000000` mapping — inferred from the switch, not measured. A miss at those offsets is still this handler (HAE at +0 is silent; `STAT0`/`STAT1` at +0x40/+0x60 hit `default:` and still kill).
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:27:**S5 does not transfer. This is the load-bearing refusal.** The live `dev = 0` path is PCI type-0 **tag decode**, not a register-value policy. A prior design pass already said so, and the source still says so: it aliases “no device selected” onto **slot 0**, which is empty today only because the installed SIO is device 7. Populate slot 0 and it is a latent alias, already filed as `lcashiftub` on the same loop. Substituting `0x700000` when firmware wrote `IOC_W_MASK_1M` (0) would be that same alias pointed at a documented encoding. **Do not cite S5 as “decline with a safe default” for these six.**
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:74:- `W_MASK0` accepts only `IOC_W_MASK_8M`. `IOC_W_MASK_1M` is `0` — documented, reset, and fatal.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:75:- `W_MASK1` accepts `IOC_W_MASK_1G`. The other eleven sizes in the same table kill.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:83:Common tail of `lca_ioc` is `memory_writemax64` on read then `return 1`. Any edit that `return`s from a case skips that. Use `break`.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:96:| TB_ENA | `idata & ~IOC_TB_ENA_TEN` | `0x80`, then `0` | same reset-0 trap |
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:98:| W_MASK0 | `!= 0x700000` | `0x700000` | `0` is **not** an accept value; it is `IOC_W_MASK_1M` and is the decline/survival pin for clause (a)/(b) |
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:116:- **Exit status cannot tell a value-guard kill from a stub kill.** That is true and is why rows match unique `fatal()` text (`IOC_CONF:`, `LCA_IOC_TB_ENA`, `W_BASE0`, `W_MASK0`, `W_BASE1`, `W_MASK1`, vs `lca_interrupt_assert: TODO`).
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:147:4. **Width is unguarded in `lca_ioc`.** Accept rows for WEN/SG constants are `stq` or they are a different (currently fatal) value. The #506 probe already had to learn that LDA/LDAH cannot build bit 32.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass1_panel\ollama_glm.txt:7:**Q2 — named premise, unsettleable: "`bus = ioc_conf & 1` is the hardware bus selector."** Internal weight [REASONED] leans to the tag: premise 3 attributes an 8-bit bus field *composed into the address* to NetBSD and mentions no register write; if hardware routed by a 1-bit register, that field would be dead bits and buses ≥2 unreachable, contradicting the comment's own multi-bus claim. But an IOC conf-register bit cannot be excluded. **Single settling fact:** the DECchip 21066 datasheet's config-cycle section — bus from address bits (AD[23:16]) or from an IOC register? (Equivalently: whether NetBSD's `lca_pci.c` writes any IOC_CONF-like register for non-zero buses; if not, address routing is the only coherent reading.) If bus-from-tag, the fix is larger *and the witness's arming step changes* (arm with a type-1 address, not an `ioc_conf` write). Note also [REASONED]: with `ioc_conf&1==0`, a type-1 tag's bus bits 16..23 fall *inside* the IDSEL scan (bits 11..31), so a NetBSD-style bus-1 access silently misdecodes as a bus-0 IDSEL dev — invisible today (empty slots return all-ones), but it means the sketch does not make type-1 decoding coherent.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass1_panel\ollama_glm.txt:13:**Q5/Q6 — not closed, and else-found.** (READ where author-named) `lca_ioc` default arm; `lca_interrupt_assert/_deassert` (filed `lcairqstubkill`). (REASONED) the `dev = 0` IDSEL fallback aliases IDSEL-less accesses onto device 0; the Q2 incoherence above; further `exit(1)`s in dev_lca.cc — I cannot enumerate them from the packet, name the grep. If implementing, replace the `fatal("TODO. Non-zero bus.")` text — the attrib row keys on it and the string becomes false. Else-found: `bus_pci_setaddr` mutates shared `pci_data` state; if any other path calls `bus_pci_data_access` without a preceding `setaddr`, an interleaved bus-1 access corrupts its routing. **Denominator: 0 call sites examined** — I am packet-fed; the only call visible to me is the inlined one. Settling fact: the call-site list of `bus_pci_setaddr`/`bus_pci_data_access`. (The decode's ignoring of addr bits 6..5, 2..0 and the `0x3<<3` marker is pre-existing, harmless — fields pack disjointly, tag ≥ bit 13, reg ≤ bit 12.)
