regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass1_panel\ollama_deepseek.txt:5:- **Q2 — READ.** The code takes `bus = d->ioc_conf & 1`; the comment says for non-zero bus the tag is `(bus << 16) | (device << 11) | (function << 8)`. These are two different sources. **Cannot settle from the packet** which is architecturally correct; need the LCA PCI configuration address spec or NetBSD `lca_pci.c`. If bus should come from the tag, the fix must extract `bus = (tag >> 16) & 0xff` and the role of `ioc_conf & 1` must be clarified.
