regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\grok_witness_20260907.txt:3:Denominator: all of `GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_lca.c` (390 lines — both handlers, `DEVINIT`, ISA, interrupt stubs); `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_pci_conf)` 89–149 in full; `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_ioc)` 182–331 in full, CONF arm 196–218; `bus_pci_data_access` / `bus_pci_setaddr` in `bus_pci.c`; `alpha_translate_v2p` K0SEG in `memory_alpha.c`; `MEMORY_RW_ONE_PAGE` device + unmapped paths in `memory_rw.c`; `LS_GENERIC_N` / `LS_N` in `cpu_alpha_instr_loadstore.c`; `fatal()` in `debugmsg.c`; `ST_ALPHABOOK1` in `machine_alpha.c`; constants in `alpha_lcareg.h`; all of `regress/lca_confwidth_probe.py`.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\grok_witness_20260907.txt:29:HAE is `case LCA_IOC_BASE:` in **`lca_ioc`**: an exact-address `break` with no store and no kill. `lca_pci_conf` has no per-offset special case. Offset 0 is `relative_addr==0` → `tag==0`, `reg==0`.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\grok_witness_20260907.txt:45:S1’s write arm (`lca_ioc`, `case LCA_IOC_CONF`) does one thing on `0x1`: `d->ioc_conf = idata;` then `idata & ~1` is 0, so no `fatal`/`exit`. An 8-byte store at `+0x020` does not overlap `STAT0` at `+0x040`. Tree-wide, `ioc_conf` is written only there and read only there (readback) and at `lca_pci_conf`’s `bus = d->ioc_conf & 1`. Nothing else can be armed by S1.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\grok_witness_20260907.txt:62:**Liveness is mislabeled.** `ioc rt` proves the **writer** (`lca_ioc` CONF) round-trips `0x1`. It does not prove S2’s window. PCI_CONF liveness is the armed session’s unique message (handler ran) plus the control surviving (same access is not an unconditional kill). If you want a positive signature on the control, the empty-slot read returns `0xffffffffffffffff` via `memory_writemax64`; unmapped returns 0. Not required for attribution.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\grok_witness_20260907.txt:91:- `STAT0`/`STAT1` error reporting (those offsets hit `lca_ioc`’s `default:` `exit(1)`).
