regress\artifacts\lcabadval\codex_disposition_20260907.txt:7960:- The header identifies LCA’s silently ignored base address as **`IOC_HAE`**, and names zero as **`IOC_W_MASK_1M`**. Thus another declared register already receives disposition 2, and the rejected zero window mask is also a named header encoding. [alpha_lcareg.h](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/alpha_lcareg.h:50).
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\codex_disposition2_20260908.txt:47:Reset alone does not establish that the guard misstates hardware behavior. There is additional local evidence against interpreting it as hardware validity: the header explicitly names zero as `IOC_W_MASK_1M`. That demonstrates a declared encoding beyond the mask guards’ accepted values; it does not establish complete register semantics. [Window-mask definitions](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/alpha_lcareg.h:85).
