regress\artifacts\lcashiftub\pass2_c7d7414\codex.txt:1167:GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:27:**S5 does not transfer. This is the load-bearing refusal.** The live `dev = 0` path is PCI type-0 **tag decode**, not a register-value policy. A prior design pass already said so, and the source still says so: it aliases “no device selected” onto **slot 0**, which is empty today only because the installed SIO is device 7. Populate slot 0 and it is a latent alias, already filed as `lcashiftub` on the same loop. Substituting `0x700000` when firmware wrote `IOC_W_MASK_1M` (0) would be that same alias pointed at a documented encoding. **Do not cite S5 as “decline with a safe default” for these six.**
regress\artifacts\lcashiftub\pass2_c7d7414\codex.txt:1168:GXEMUL-SEC/regress\artifacts\lcabadval\grok_design_20260907.txt:135:A detector that only writes the six currently-legal constants is green under **verbatim reinstatement of all six original guards**. That is the vacuity-floor miss. The rows that make (b) bite are the documented-rejected writes (MASK0 `0`, BASE1 with WEN clear, CONF bit 32, a non-TEN TB_ENA bit).
