10533:6.4.9 Window Base Registers
10534:
10535:            There is one window base (IOC_W_BASE) register for each PCI target
10536:            window. These registers (IOC_W_BASE1, IOC_W_BASE0) specify the starting
10537:            addresses of the PCI target windows in PCI memory address space. The
10538:            window base addresses must be on a naturally aligned address boundary
10539:            equal to the window's size. Additionally, to ensure that only one PCI target
10540:            window can match an incoming PCI address, the PCI target windows must be
10541:            programmed so that they do not respond to overlapping PCI address ranges.
10542:            (See Section 6.3.2 for more information about using these registers.)
10543:
10544:            Software should ensure that the PCI is idle before updating these registers.
10545:
10546:            The IOC_W_BASE0 register is accessed at address 18000010016 and the
10547:            IOC_W_BASE1 register is accessed at address 18000012016. All bits of these
10548:            registers are UNDEFINED after reset.
10549:
10550:            Figure 6-9 shows the IOC_W_BASE register format, and Table 6-16 describes
10551:            its fields.
10552:
10553:                                                   I/O Controller 6-45
10554:Figure 6-9 IOC_W_BASE1-0 Registers Format
10555:
10556:63                            34 33 32 31             20 19       0
10557:
10558:                     RES      W  S          W_BASE           RES
10559:                              E  G           <31:20>
10560:                              N
10561:
10562:Table 6-16 IOC_W_BASE1-0 Registers Field Description
10563:
10564:Bits Field                Type Description
10565:
10566:63:34 RES                 X   Reserved.
10567:
10568:33     WEN                WO  Window enable--When this bit is set, the PCI target
10569:                              window is enabled and responds to PCI-initiated
10570:32     SG                 WO  transfers that hit in the address range of the target
10571:                              window. When this bit is clear, the PCI target window is
10572:31:20  W_BASE WO              disabled and does not respond to PCI-initiated transfers.
10573:19:0   <31:20>
10574:                              Scatter-gather--When this bit is set, the PCI target
10575:       RES                X   window uses scatter-gather mapping to translate a PCI
10576:                              address to a CPU address. When this bit is clear, the
10577:                              PCI target window uses direct mapping to translate a
10578:                              PCI address to a CPU address.
10579:
10580:                              Window base--This field specifies the starting address
10581:                              of the PCI target window in PCI memory address space.
10582:
10583:                              Reserved.
10584:
10585:6.4.10 Window Mask Registers
10586:
10587:            There is one window mask (IOC_W_MASK) register for each PCI target
10588:            window. These registers (IOC_W_MASK1, IOC_W_MASK0) provide a mask
10589:            that corresponds to incoming PCI address bits <31:20>. The mask determines
10590:            the size of the PCI target window. (See Section 6.3.2 for more information
10591:            about using these registers.)
10592:
10593:            Software should ensure that the PCI is idle before updating these registers.
10594:
10595:            The IOC_W_MASK0 register is accessed at address 18000014016 and the
10596:            IOC_W_MASK1 register is accessed at address 18000016016. All bits of these
10597:            registers are UNDEFINED after reset.
10598:
10599:            Figure 6-10 shows the IOC_W_MASK register format, and Table 6-17
10600:            describes its fields.
10601:
10602:6-46 I/O Controller
10603:Figure 6-10 IOC_W_MASK1-0 Registers Format
10604:
10605:63                32 31                     20 19          0
10606:
10607:            RES               W_MASK                  RES
10608:                                <31:20>
10609:
10610:Table 6-17 IOC_W_MASK1-0 Registers Field Description
10611:
10612:Bits Field  Type Description
10613:
10614:63:32  RES  X     Reserved.
10615:31:20
10616:       W_MASK WO  Window mask--This field specifies the size of the PCI
10617:       <31:20>    target window. It can also mask the address bits that
10618:                  are not used when translating the PCI address to the
10619:19:0 RES    X     CPU address to determine whether an address matches
10620:                  the PCI target window address range.
10621:
10622:                  Reserved.
10623:
10624:6.4.11 Translated Base Registers
10624:6.4.11 Translated Base Registers
10625:
10626:            There is one translated base (IOC_T_BASE) register for each PCI target
10627:            window.
10628:
10629:            When direct-mapped address translation is used, the translated address is
10630:            generated by concatenating bits from an IOC_T_BASE register with bits from
10631:            the incoming PCI address. The IOC_W_MASK register determines which
10632:            IOC_T_BASE register bits and PCI address bits are concatenated to form the
10633:            translated address. The translated address is the starting address in system
10634:            memory for the PCI transaction.
10635:
10636:            When scatter-gather mapped address translation is used, the translated
10637:            address is generated by table lookup. The table (scatter-gather map) is stored
10638:            in system memory. The IOC_T_BASE register specifies the starting address
10639:            of the scatter-gather map, and the incoming PCI address bits are used as an
10640:            offset from that address. (See Sections 6.3.2.1 and 6.3.2.2 for more information
10641:            about using these registers.)
10642:
10643:            Software should ensure that the PCI is idle before updating these registers.
10644:
10645:            The IOC_T_BASE0 register is accessed at address 18000018016 and the
10646:            IOC_T_BASE1 register is accessed at address 1800001A0. All bits of these
10647:            registers are UNDEFINED after reset.
10648:
10649:                                                      I/O Controller 6-47
10650:Figure 6-11 shows the IOC_T_BASE register format, and Table 6-18 describes
10651:its fields.
10652:
10653:Figure 6-11 IOC_T_BASE1-0 Registers Format
10654:
10655:63                        32 31                       10 9       0
10656:
10657:                     RES                    T_BASE          RES
10658:                                            <31:10>
10659:
10660:Table 6-18 IOC_T_BASE1-0 Registers Field Description
10661:
10662:Bits Field           Type Description
10663:
10664:63:32 RES            X    Reserved.
10665:
10666:31:10 T_BASE WO           Translation base--When scatter-gather mapping is
10667:             <31:10>      enabled, this field specifies the base address in system
10668:                          memory for the scatter-gather map. When scatter-
10669:9:0  RES             X    gather mapping is disabled, this field and the incoming
10670:                          PCI address are concatenated to form the translated
10671:                          address.
10672:
10673:                          Reserved.
10674:
10675:6.4.12 Translation Buffer Tag Registers
10676:
10677:            There is one translation buffer tag (IOC_TB_TAG) register for each TLB entry.
10678:            The IOC automatically updates these registers (IOC_TB_TAG7-0) when all of
10679:            the following conditions are met:
10680:
10681:            � The TEN bit is set in the IOC_TB_ENA register (Section 6.4.6).
10682:
10683:            � A PCI transaction hits in a PCI target window.
10684:
10685:            � The WEN and SG bits are both set in the IOC_W_BASE register
10686:                  (Section 6.4.9) associated with the PCI target window.
10687:
10688:            The IOC_TB_TAG registers can also be written directly for diagnostic purposes.
10689:
10690:            See Section 6.3.3 for more information about the TLB.
10691:
10692:            The IOC_TB_TAG registers can be accessed at the following addresses:
10693:
10694:6-48 I/O Controller
10695:Register              Address
10696:
10697:IOC_TB_TAG0           188000000
10698:IOC_TB_TAG1           188000020
10699:IOC_TB_TAG2           188000040
10700:IOC_TB_TAG3           188000060
10701:IOC_TB_TAG4           188000080
10702:IOC_TB_TAG5           1880000A0
10703:IOC_TB_TAG6           1880000C0
10704:IOC_TB_TAG7           1880000E0
10705:
10706:All bits of these registers are UNDEFINED after reset.
10707:
10708:Figure 6-12 shows the IOC_TB_TAG register format, and Table 6-19 describes
10709:its fields.
10710:
10711:Figure 6-12 IOC_TB_TAG7-0 Registers Format
10712:
10713:63                               32 31                13 12                   0
10714:
10715:             RES                        TB_TAG               RES
10716:                                        <31:13>
10717:
10718:Table 6-19 IOC_TB_TAG7-0 Registers Field Description
10719:
10720:Bits Field   Type Description
10721:
10722:63:32 RES    X        Reserved.
10723:
10724:31:13 TB_TAG WO       Translation buffer tag--This field provides write-only
10725:             <31:13>  access to one of eight TLB tags.
10726:
10727:12:0 RES     X        Reserved.
10728:
10729:6.4.13 Interrupt Vector and Special Cycle Register
10730:
10731:            When the interrupt vector and special cycle (IOC_IACK_SC) register is read,
10732:            the IOC generates an interrupt acknowledge cycle on the PCI bus and returns
10733:            the vector data provided by external logic as the read data to the CPU.
10734:
10735:            When the IOC_IACK_SC register is written, the IOC generates a PCI transfer
10736:            with a special cycle command code. The data written to the register is
10737:            transferred unmodified to the PCI bus and contains the special message data.
10738:
10739:                                                      I/O Controller 6-49
10740:                                                   Note
10741:
10742:    Digital recommends that software use only address 1A0000000 to
10743:    reference the IOC_IACK_SC register. However, in the current
10744:    chip implementation, CPU address bits <28:0> are not decoded to
10745:    access the IOC_IACK_SC register, and any address in the range
10746:    1A0000000..1BFFFFFE0 will alias to this single register. For
10747:    implementation convenience, the chip will drive the supplied address
10748:    onto the PCI bus.
10749:
10750:All bits of the IOC_IACK_SC register are UNDEFINED after reset.
10751:
10752:Figure 6-13 shows the IOC_IACK_SC register format, and Table 6-20
10753:describes its fields.
10754:
10755:Figure 6-13 IOC_IACK_SC Register Format
10756:
10757:63                                   32 31                                   0
10758:
10759:                     RES                           Data
10760:
10761:Table 6-20 IOC_IACK_SC Register Field Description
10762:
10763:Bits Field           Type Description
10764:
10765:63:32  RES           X    Reserved.
