9561:6.3.2 PCI Address Translation
9562:
9563:            Because the PCI uses a 32-bit address and the CPU uses a 34-bit address,
9564:            PCI addresses to which the IOC responds must be translated to an equivalent
9565:            address in the CPU address space. The IOC implements two programmable
9566:            address windows, called PCI target windows, that control PCI peripheral access
9567:            to system memory. A set of three IOC registers is associated with each PCI
9568:            target window: the window base; window mask; and translated base registers
9569:            (IOC_W_BASE<1:0>, Section 6.4.9; IOC_W_MASK<1:0>, Section 6.4.10; and
9570:            IOC_T_BASE<1:0>, Section 6.4.11).
9571:
9572:            The window mask register IOC_W_MASK provides a mask corresponding
9573:            to bits <31:20> of an incoming PCI address. The size of each window is
9574:            programmed to be from 1 MB to 4 GB by masking bits of the incoming PCI
9575:            address with the IOC_W_MASK register.
9576:
9577:            Table 6-6 shows the supported values of IOC_W_MASK register bits <31:20>;
9578:            other values are unsupported.
9579:
9580:                                                   I/O Controller 6-23
9581:Table 6-6 PCI Window Mask
9582:
9583:IOC_W_MASK           Window
9584:        <31:20>         Size
9585:
9586:0000 0000 0000          1 MB
9587:0000 0000 0001          2 MB
9588:0000 0000 0011          4 MB
9589:0000 0000 0111          8 MB
9590:0000 0000 1111        16 MB
9591:0000 0001 1111        32 MB
9592:0000 0011 1111        64 MB
9593:0000 0111 1111       128 MB
9594:0000 1111 1111       256 MB
9595:0001 1111 1111       512 MB
9596:0011 1111 1111          1 GB
9597:0111 1111 1111          2 GB
9598:1111 1111 1111          4 GB
9599:
9600:IOC_W_BASE register bits <31:20> specify the target window starting address
9601:in the PCI memory address space. The IOC_W_BASE and IOC_W_MASK
9602:registers determine when a PCI transaction references an address in a target
9603:window, as follows:
9604:
9605:1. Each of the incoming PCI address bits <31:20> is exclusive-ORed with
9606:     the corresponding bit of each window base register (IOC_W_BASE1,
9607:     IOC_W_BASE0, bits <31:20>).
9608:
9609:2. The result of each exclusive-OR is then ANDed with the complement
9610:     of the corresponding bits of the corresponding window mask register
9611:     (IOC_W_MASK1, IOC_W_MASK0, bits <31:20>).
9612:
9613:3. The result of the AND operation for each window is then ORed to produce
9614:     a hit (match) or miss indication. If the result of the final OR is a zero for
9615:     a given window, the incoming address has hit in that PCI target window;
9616:     otherwise, it has missed in that window.
9617:
9618:                                                    Note
9619:
9620:     The window base address must be on a naturally aligned address
9621:     boundary equal to the window size (Table 6-6). Additionally, to ensure
9622:     that only one PCI target window can match an incoming PCI address,
9623:     the PCI target windows must be programmed so that they do not
9624:     respond to overlapping PCI address ranges.
9625:
9626:6-24 I/O Controller
9627:            Each target window is independently enabled when the window enable bit
9628:            (WEN) is set in the corresponding IOC_W_BASE register. The IOC responds
9629:            only to PCI-initiated transfers that hit in an enabled window. If the WEN bit
9630:            is cleared, the IOC ignores PCI-initiated transfers that hit in that window.
9631:            When a hit occurs in an enabled PCI target window, the IOC responds to
9632:            the PCI cycle by asserting the devsel_l signal. The IOC translates the
9633:            32-bit PCI address to a 34-bit CPU address. The scatter-gather (SG) bit
9634:            in the corresponding IOC_W_BASE register determines how the address
9635:            is translated. If the SG bit is clear, direct-mapped address translation is
9636:            used (Section 6.3.2.1). If the SG bit is set, scatter-gather mapped address
9637:            translation is used (Section 6.3.2.2).
9638:6.3.2.1 Direct-Mapped Address Translation
9639:            Direct-mapped address translation is used when an incoming PCI address
9640:            hits in a PCI target window and the SG bit is not set in the corresponding
9641:            IOC_W_BASE register. The translated address is generated by concatenating
9642:            bits from the corresponding IOC_T_BASE register with bits from the incoming
9643:            PCI address. Bits <33:32> of the translated address are always zero. The
9644:            IOC_W_MASK register determines which IOC_T_BASE register bits and PCI
9645:            address bits are concatenated to form the translated address, as shown in
9646:            Table 6-7. The translated address is the starting address in system memory
9647:            for the PCI transaction.
9648:
9649:                                                               Caution
9650:                  Unused bits of the translated base register must be clear (zero) for
9651:                  correct operation.
9652:
9653:                                                                                                               I/O Controller 6-25
9654:Table 6-7 PCI Address Translation--Scatter-Gather Mapping Disabled
9655:
9656:IOC_W_MASK           Translated Address <31:0>  Unused
9657:
9658:<31:20>              IOC_T_BASE  PCI Address IOC_T_BASE
9659:
9660:0000 0000 0000       <31:20>     <19:0>         <19:9>
9661:0000 0000 0001       <31:21>     <20:0>         <20:9>
9662:0000 0000 0011       <31:22>     <21:0>         <21:9>
9663:0000 0000 0111       <31:23>     <22:0>         <22:9>
9664:0000 0000 1111       <31:24>     <23:0>         <23:9>
9665:0000 0001 1111       <31:25>     <24:0>         <24:9>
9666:0000 0011 1111       <31:26>     <25:0>         <25:9>
9667:0000 0111 1111       <31:27>     <26:0>         <26:9>
9668:0000 1111 1111       <31:28>     <27:0>         <27:9>
9669:0001 1111 1111       <31:29>     <28:0>         <28:9>
9670:0011 1111 1111       <31:30>     <29:0>         <29:9>
9671:0111 1111 1111       <31>        <30:0>         <30:9>
9672:1111 1111 1111       --          <31:0>         <31:9>
9673:
9674:6.3.2.2 Scatter-Gather Mapped Address Translation
9675:
9676:            Scatter-gather mapped address translation is used when an incoming PCI
9677:            address hits in a PCI target window and the SG bit is set in the corresponding
9678:            IOC_W_BASE register. The translated address is generated by table lookup.
9679:            The table is called a scatter-gather map and is stored in system memory. The
9680:            IOC combines the incoming PCI address with the corresponding IOC_T_BASE
9681:            register to generate the index address into the scatter-gather map. The
9682:            IOC_T_BASE register specifies the starting address of the scatter-gather map,
9683:            and the incoming PCI address bits are used as an offset from that address.
9684:
9685:            The size of the PCI target window, as defined by the IOC_W_MASK register,
9686:            determines the length of the scatter-gather map, as shown in Table 6-8. Each
9687:            scatter-gather map entry maps an 8-KB page of the PCI address space into an
9688:            8-KB page of the CPU address space.
9689:
9690:            The IOC_W_MASK register determines which IOC_T_BASE register bits and
9691:            PCI address bits generate the address of the scatter-gather map entry, as
9692:            shown in Table 6-8. Translated address bits <33:32> are always zero, and
9693:            because each scatter-gather map entry is a quadword (64 bits), the three
9694:            LSBs (<2:0>) of a scatter-gather map address are also always zero. The
9695:            resultant address is used to read an entry from the scatter-gather map in
9696:            system memory.
9697:
9698:6-26 I/O Controller
9699:                                                      Caution
9700:
9701:         Unused IOC_T_BASE register bits must be clear (zero) for correct
9702:         operation.
9703:
9704:Table 6-8 Scatter-Gather Map Address
9705:
9706:IOC_W_MASK Scatter-Gather  Translated Address <31:0>          Unused
9707:
9708:<31:20>         Map Size IOC_T_BASE PCI Address <2:0>      IOC_T_BASE
9709:
9710:0000 0000 0000     1 KB    <31:10>    <19:13>         000        None
9711:0000 0000 0001     2 KB    <31:11>                               <10>
9712:0000 0000 0011     4 KB    <31:12>    <20:13>         000      <11:10>
9713:0000 0000 0111     8 KB    <31:13>                             <12:10>
9714:0000 0000 1111   26 KB     <31:14>    <21:13>         000      <13:10>
9715:0000 0001 1111   32 KB     <31:15>                             <14:10>
9716:0000 0011 1111   64 KB     <31:16>    <22:13>         000      <15:10>
9717:0000 0111 1111  128 KB     <31:17>                             <16:10>
9718:0000 1111 1111  256 KB     <31:18>    <23:13>         000      <17:10>
9719:0001 1111 1111  512 KB     <31:19>                             <18:10>
9720:0011 1111 1111     1 MB    <31:20>    <24:13>         000      <19:10>
9721:0111 1111 1111     2 MB    <31:21>                             <20:10>
9722:1111 1111 1111     4 MB    <31:22>    <25:13>         000      <21:10>
9723:
9724:                                      <26:13>         000
9725:
9726:                                      <27:13>         000
9727:
9728:                                      <28:13>         000
9729:
9730:                                      <29:13>         000
9731:
9732:                                      <30:13>         000
9733:
9734:                                      <31:13>         000
9735:
9736:The scatter-gather map entry read from system memory specifies a page
9737:address in the 34-bit CPU address space. Because the page size is 8 KB and
9738:translated address bits <33:32> are always zero, the page table entry (PTE)
9739:specifies only address bits <31:13>.
9740:
10175:6.4 I/O Controller Registers
10176:
10177:            The IOC implements a number of registers to control its operation and
10178:            facilitate its testing. The CPU can access the IOC registers directly, but they
10179:            are not accessible from the PCI bus.
10180:            All references to the IOC registers must allow for quadword access; longword
10181:            access is not supported.
10182:            The IOC registers are described in ascending-address order in Sections 6.4.1
10183:            through 6.4.14. Unless stated otherwise, the assertion of reset_in_l does not
10184:            modify any IOC register bits and all IOC register bits are UNDEFINED after
10185:            a power-up reset.
10186:
10187:                                                                 Note
10188:                  In the register field description tables, the abbreviations in the Type
10189:                  column indicate field access behavior. The abbreviations are defined in
10190:                  the Conventions section of the Preface.
10191:
10192:                                                                                                               I/O Controller 6-37
10193:6.4.1 Host Address Extension Register
10194:
10195:            In the sparse memory space, the lower bits of the CPU address indicate
10196:            transfer size, and the address is shifted down by 5 bits during the translation
10197:            from CPU address to PCI address. The host address extension (IOC_HAE)
10198:            register extends the shifted address to 32 bits.
10199:
10200:            The IOC_HAE register is accessed at address 18000000016. All bits of this
10201:            register are UNDEFINED after reset.
10202:
10203:            Figure 6-2 shows the IOC_HAE register format, and Table 6-9 describes its
10204:            fields.
10205:
10206:Figure 6-2 IOC_HAE Register Format
10207:
10208:63                        32 31 27 26              0
10209:
10210:                     RES             HAE      RES
10211:                                    <31:27>
10212:
10213:Table 6-9 IOC_HAE Register Field Description
10214:
10215:Bits Field           Type Description
10216:
10217:63:32  RES           X    Reserved.
10218:31:27
10219:       HAE<31:27> WO      Host address extension--This field is used for PCI
10220:                          address bits ad<31:27> during CPU-initiated PCI
10221:26:0 RES             X    transactions when CPU physical address bits <31:29>
10222:                          are non-zero (see Table 6-1).
10223:
10224:                          Reserved.
10225:
10226:6.4.2 Configuration Cycle Type Register
10227:
10228:            During CPU-initiated PCI configuration space transfers, the configuration cycle
10229:            type (IOC_CONF) register supplies PCI address bits ad<1:0>.
10230:
10231:            The IOC_CONF register is accessed at address 18000002016. All bits of this
10232:            register are UNDEFINED after reset.
10233:
10234:            Figure 6-3 shows the IOC_CONF register format, and Table 6-10 describes its
10235:            fields.
10236:
10237:6-38 I/O Controller
10238:Figure 6-3 IOC_CONF Register Format                         210
10239:
10240: 63                                                            CFG
10241:                                                                AD
10242:                                                       RES    <1:0>
10243:
10244:Table 6-10 IOC_CONF Register Field Description
10245:
10246:Bits Field    Type Description
10247:
10248:63:2 RES      X   Reserved.
10249:
10250:1:0  CFG      WO  Configuration address-- This field is used as PCI
10251:
10252:     AD<1:0>      address bits ad<1:0> during CPU-initiated PCI
10253:
10254:                  configuration cycles.
10255:
10256:6.4.3 Status 0 Register
10257:
10411:6.4.5 Translation Buffer Invalidate All Register
10412:
10413:            A write operation to the translation buffer invalidate all (IOC_TBIA) register
10414:            invalidates all entries in the scatter-gather map TLB at the start of the next
10415:            PCI-initiated transaction (Section 6.3.3).
10416:
10417:            The IOC_TBIA register is accessed at address 18000008016. All bits of this
10418:            register are reserved and are ignored on write operations and UNDEFINED on
10419:            read operations.
10420:
10421:6-42 I/O Controller
10422:6.4.6 Translation Buffer Enable Register
10423:
10424:            The translation buffer enable (IOC_TB_ENA) register determines whether the
10425:            scatter-gather map TLB is enabled (Section 6.3.3).
10426:
10427:            The IOC_TB_ENA register is accessed at address 1800000A0. All bits of this
10428:            register are UNDEFINED after reset.
10429:
10430:            Figure 6-6 shows the IOC_TB_ENA register format, and Table 6-13 describes
10431:            its fields.
10432:
10433:Figure 6-6 IOC_TB_ENA Register Format             876              0
10434:
10435: 63                                               T
10436:                                                  E RES
10437:                                            RES   N
10438:
10439:Table 6-13 IOC_TB_ENA Register Field Description
10440:
10441:Bits Field  Type Description
10442:
10443:63:8 RES    X   Reserved.
10444:
10445:7    TEN    WO  TLB enable--When written with a zero, this bit disables
10446:
10447:                the scatter-gather map TLB. The TLB remains disabled
10448:
10449:                until this bit is written with a one. Disabling the TLB
10450:
10451:                does not disable scatter-gather map translations.
10452:
