1001:    Bit Notation
1002:
1003:    Multiple-bit fields can include contiguous and noncontiguous bits contained
1004:    in angle brackets ( <> ). Multiple contiguous bits are indicated by a pair of
1005:    numbers separated by a colon ( : ). For example, <9:7,5,2:0> specifies bits
1006:    9,8,7,5,2,1, and 0. Similarly, single bit positions are frequently indicated with
1007:    angle brackets. For example, ``The PAL bit (<0>) indicates PALmode to the
1008:    hardware,'' indicates that the PAL bit is bit 0 in a register.1
