10422:6.4.6 Translation Buffer Enable Register
10423:
10424:            The translation buffer enable (IOC_TB_ENA) register determines whether the
10425:            scatter-gather map TLB is enabled (Section 6.3.3).
10426:
10427:            The IOC_TB_ENA register is accessed at address 1800000A0. All bits of this
10428:            register are UNDEFINED after reset.
10429:
10430:            Figure 6-6 shows the IOC_TB_ENA register format, and Table 6-13 describes
10431:            its fields.
10432:
10433:Figure 6-6 IOC_TB_ENA Register Format             876              0
10434:
10435: 63                                               T
10436:                                                  E RES
10437:                                            RES   N
10438:
10439:Table 6-13 IOC_TB_ENA Register Field Description
10440:
10441:Bits Field  Type Description
10442:
10443:63:8 RES    X   Reserved.
10444:
10445:7    TEN    WO  TLB enable--When written with a zero, this bit disables
10446:
10447:                the scatter-gather map TLB. The TLB remains disabled
10448:
10449:                until this bit is written with a one. Disabling the TLB
10450:
10451:                does not disable scatter-gather map translations.
10452:
10453:6:0  RES    X   Reserved.
10454:
10455:6.4.7 PCI Soft Reset Register
10533:6.4.9 Window Base Registers
10534:
10535:            There is one window base (IOC_W_BASE) register for each PCI target
10536:            window. These registers (IOC_W_BASE1, IOC_W_BASE0) specify the starting
10537:            addresses of the PCI target windows in PCI memory address space. The
10538:            window base addresses must be on a naturally aligned address boundary
10539:            equal to the window's size. Additionally, to ensure that only one PCI target
10540:            window can match an incoming PCI address, the PCI target windows must be
10541:            programmed so that they do not respond to overlapping PCI address ranges.
10542:            (See Section 6.3.2 for more information about using these registers.)
10543:
10544:            Software should ensure that the PCI is idle before updating these registers.
10545:
10546:            The IOC_W_BASE0 register is accessed at address 18000010016 and the
10547:            IOC_W_BASE1 register is accessed at address 18000012016. All bits of these
10548:            registers are UNDEFINED after reset.
10549:
10550:            Figure 6-9 shows the IOC_W_BASE register format, and Table 6-16 describes
10551:            its fields.
10552:
10553:                                                   I/O Controller 6-45
10554:Figure 6-9 IOC_W_BASE1-0 Registers Format
10555:
10556:63                            34 33 32 31             20 19       0
10557:
10558:                     RES      W  S          W_BASE           RES
10559:                              E  G           <31:20>
10560:                              N
10561:
10562:Table 6-16 IOC_W_BASE1-0 Registers Field Description
10563:
10564:Bits Field                Type Description
10565:
10566:63:34 RES                 X   Reserved.
10567:
10568:33     WEN                WO  Window enable--When this bit is set, the PCI target
10569:                              window is enabled and responds to PCI-initiated
10570:32     SG                 WO  transfers that hit in the address range of the target
10571:                              window. When this bit is clear, the PCI target window is
10572:31:20  W_BASE WO              disabled and does not respond to PCI-initiated transfers.
10573:19:0   <31:20>
10574:                              Scatter-gather--When this bit is set, the PCI target
10575:       RES                X   window uses scatter-gather mapping to translate a PCI
10576:                              address to a CPU address. When this bit is clear, the
