The reserved fields are marked `X`, which the manual defines as ignored on writes. That changes the TB_ENA finding: the fork accepts both TEN states, but terminates on bits hardware ignores. The six arms also already store the value before checking it, and the fork has concrete `(once)` latch examples for nonterminating declines.
