180:/*
181: *  #451: the two command-byte validators in sh4_sci_cmd().  This site is not reached
182: *  DIRECTLY BY A SINGLE REGISTER STORE: the guest must CLOCK a byte in, bit by bit,
183: *  through SHREG_SCSPTR -- seventeen ordinary mov.b stores -- and only the eighth rising
184: *  edge calls sh4_sci_cmd(), which ended the host on a byte it does not implement.
185: *  (An earlier draft said "unlike every SH-4 site before it", which contradicts the
186: *  #449 block a few lines above: RTCSRINT is not reached from a store either.  It is
187: *  reached from a timer callback.  The distinction that actually holds is single-store
188: *  versus multi-store PROTOCOL.)
189: *
